Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and potential usage

PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS  
• "country_code": filter to Chinese (CN) patents.  
• "grant_date": numeric YYYYMMDD; select grants between 20100101‑20231231.  
• "family_id": groups all documents belonging to one simple family; needed for counting per family.  
• "application_number" / "application_number_formatted": identify distinct applications inside each family.  
• "publication_date": sometimes helpful to cross‑check the time window when no grant date is present.  
• "kind_code": may be used to keep only granted documents (e.g., B‑kind, but we will first look at the values).  
• "application_kind": could restrict to patents (“A”) if necessary.  

Typical conditions we may need

1. "country_code" = 'CN'  
2. "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231  
3. Families whose COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1  

Exploratory / building‑block queries
(Every query LIMITs to 20 rows to sample values.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Inspect a few Chinese publications to understand grant and application kinds
SELECT "publication_number",
       "kind_code",
       "application_kind",
       "grant_date",
       "publication_date",
       "country_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) View some rows that actually have a non‑zero grant_date in China after 2010
SELECT "publication_number",
       "grant_date",
       "kind_code",
       "family_id"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Check distribution of kind_code for granted Chinese records
SELECT DISTINCT "kind_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Sample the application numbers inside a family to verify there can be >1 distinct values
SELECT "family_id",
       "application_number",
       "application_number_formatted"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "family_id" = (
        SELECT "family_id"
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
        WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
          AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
        LIMIT 1
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Identify families (limited sample) that appear to have more than one distinct application number
SELECT "family_id",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") AS "distinct_apps"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
GROUP BY "family_id"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) For those multi‑application families, list the individual applications and dates
SELECT p."family_id",
       p."application_number",
       p."application_number_formatted",
       p."grant_date"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
JOIN (
     SELECT "family_id"
     FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
     WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
       AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
     GROUP BY "family_id"
     HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1
     LIMIT 20 -- sample
) f
ON p."family_id" = f."family_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count how many granted Chinese documents (not yet families) fall in period 2010‑2023
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "cn_granted_2010_2023"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Aggregate to families and count families with >1 applications (full count, but limit shows partial)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "families_gt1_app"
FROM (
     SELECT "family_id"
     FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
     WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
       AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
     GROUP BY "family_id"
     HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1
) fam
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Retrieve distinct publication_numbers inside qualifying families to see volume
SELECT DISTINCT "publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "family_id" IN (
      SELECT "family_id"
      FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
      WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
        AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
      GROUP BY "family_id"
      HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1
 )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL query template to answer: number of granted Chinese patents 2010‑2023 whose families contain >1 distinct applications
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "cn_granted_patents_in_families_with_gt1_app"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
WHERE p."country_code" = 'CN'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
  AND p."family_id" IN (
        SELECT "family_id"
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
        WHERE "country_code" = 'CN'
          AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20231231
        GROUP BY "family_id"
        HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "application_number") > 1
     )
LIMIT 20;
```
